From 13fdbb98b0d426642548f410cb48775e6af515d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Mausberg <samuelmausberg@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 06:40:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] Route Qwen3.5 backbone projections through the skinny
 GEMM (opt-in)

Every switch defaults to off, and with all of them off no code path changes.
- SGLANG_BACKBONE_GEMM=1: UnquantizedLinearMethod.apply and
  _bf16_gemm_dispatch_impl send bias-free BF16 projections whose (N, K, M) has
  a table entry to the skinny GEMM (table from SGLANG_BACKBONE_GEMM_TABLE).
- SGLANG_BACKBONE_MERGE_IN_PROJ=1: Qwen3.5's GDN layers pack in_proj_qkvz and
  in_proj_ba into one weight on CUDA too (it was finalized only under aiter),
  and the dense Qwen3_5ForConditionalGeneration forwards
  prepare_before_cuda_graph_capture to its language model, as the MoE wrapper
  already does.
- SGLANG_BACKBONE_FUSE_ACT=1: Qwen2MoeMLP folds SiLU-mul into the down
  projection's prologue (plain TP=1 BF16 only).
- SGLANG_BACKBONE_FUSE_NORM=1: the plain residual readouts may defer the add
  and Gemma RMSNorm into the next projection's prologue (DeferredNormInput),
  never on aux hidden-state capture layers or under LoRA.
